From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h700: blinking sleep LED on every board

Every H700 board has its power LED on PI12, which can be muxed to PWM2.
Move the rumble/power-LED coordinator from the RG35XX Pro and RG40XX-V
device trees into the shared rumble includes, so the power LED blinks
during sleep (s2idle or deep) on the whole family:

- sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm2-rumble.dtsi (motor on PWM2/PH2): the
  "anbernic,rg35xx-pro-haptics" coordinator replaces pwm-vibrator.
- sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm3-rumble-pi13.dtsi (RG40XX-H/V, RG CubeXX,
  motor on PWM3/PI13): the "anbernic,rg40xx-v-power-led" coordinator
  owns the PWM2/PWM3 pair instead.

The gpio-leds power LED is dropped where the coordinator takes PI12.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm2-rumble.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm2-rumble.dtsi
@@ -3,14 +3,47 @@
 /*
  * Vibration motor on PWM2 (PH2), the route of the boards that keep PH2
  * free (no RGB controller on UART5), as ROCKNIX describes the family.
+ *
+ * nuubOS: PI12, the power LED of every H700 board, can be muxed to PWM2
+ * too, so one coordinator owns PWM2, the motor and the power LED:
+ *
+ * runtime:
+ *   PH2  -> PWM2 -> vibration motor
+ *   PI12 -> GPIO -> power LED
+ *
+ * sleep (s2idle or deep):
+ *   PH2  -> GPIO input
+ *   PI12 -> PWM2 -> blinking power LED
  */
+&pio {
+	pwm2_pi12_pin: pwm2-pi12-pin {
+		pins = "PI12";
+		function = "pwm2";
+	};
+
+	ph2_gpio_in_pin: ph2-gpio-in-pin {
+		pins = "PH2";
+		function = "gpio_in";
+	};
+};
+
+&{/leds} {
+	/* Owned by the coordinator below. */
+	/delete-node/ led-0;
+};
+
 / {
-	pwm-vibrator {
-		compatible = "pwm-vibrator";
+	haptics_led {
+		compatible = "anbernic,rg35xx-pro-haptics";
+
+		pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pwm2_pin>;
+		pinctrl-1 = <&ph2_gpio_in_pin>, <&pwm2_pi12_pin>;
+
+		power-led-gpios = <&pio 8 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PI12 */
+
 		pwms = <&pwm 2 1000000 0>;
 		pwm-names = "enable";
-		pinctrl-names = "default";
-		pinctrl-0 = <&pwm2_pin>;
 	};
 };
 
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm3-rumble-pi13.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm3-rumble-pi13.dtsi
@@ -1,10 +1,13 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
 
-#include "sun50i-h700-anbernic-pwm3-rumble.dtsi"
-
 /*
- * Shared PI13 PWM3 routing used by the RG40XX-V and RG CubeXX.
- * PH0 is reserved by UART0 on these boards.
+ * Shared PI13 PWM3 routing used by the RG40XX-H/V and RG CubeXX.
+ * PH0 is reserved by UART0 on these boards, PH2 by the RGB UART5.
+ *
+ * nuubOS: the motor moves to PWM3, PWM2 only blinks the PI12 power LED
+ * during sleep. Both channels share the pair clock on H616/H700, so one
+ * coordinator owns the whole PWM2/PWM3 pair instead of the PWM2 one of
+ * the base board.
  */
 &pio {
 	pwm3_pi13_pin: pwm3-pi13-pin {
@@ -13,6 +16,20 @@
 	};
 };
 
-&{/pwm-vibrator} {
-	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm3_pi13_pin>;
+/ {
+	/delete-node/ haptics_led;
+
+	suspend_power_led {
+		compatible = "anbernic,rg40xx-v-power-led";
+
+		pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pwm3_pi13_pin>;
+		pinctrl-1 = <&pwm2_pi12_pin>;
+
+		power-led-gpios = <&pio 8 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PI12 */
+
+		pwms = <&pwm 2 3000000000 0>,
+		       <&pwm 3 1000000 0>;
+		pwm-names = "sleep-led", "rumble";
+	};
 };
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-pro.dts
@@ -44,23 +44,6 @@
 	};
 };
 
